<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Results</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Thinking models excel in chat and creative writing.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Baselines and algorithms. ‣ 3.1 Settings, Benchmarks and Evaluated Models ‣ 3 Thinking Benefits Open-ended Reasoning ‣ Language Models that Think, Chat Better" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> contains results after SFT, and after GRPO for both thinking and non-thinking models.
Thinking models trained with RLMT consistently outperform non-thinking counterparts by 1.5–4 points on average across all benchmarks (Tables <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Baselines and algorithms. ‣ 3.1 Settings, Benchmarks and Evaluated Models ‣ 3 Thinking Benefits Open-ended Reasoning ‣ Language Models that Think, Chat Better" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
